 "findings": [
  {
   "id": "F1",
   "severity": "high",
   "scope": "all w > 0 candidate-vs-baseline ratios and baseline distance-to-rho at w > 0",
   "finding": "`residual_table_bytes_uncharged` (residual.rs:493-496, table.len()*(16+8*d_col) bytes) is named *_uncharged, so it enters cost.unpriced and band.rs sums it as if it were an operation count at weight w. For the baseline arms it is the dominant w>0 term (bytes counter share of priced cost at w=1: see bytes_counter_share). work.rs classes the analogous native_table_bytes_uncharged as `Shape` (not work). Candidates store only distinguished points, so their byte counter is about 150-210x smaller (e.g. p36 res1 7.04M vs res1dp 47.5k vs res1eq 33.4k bytes on average); the w>0 candidate/baseline advantage is largely this memory reduction priced at 1 GAE per byte (AGENTS.md section 6: a ratio improved by changing the unit does not count).",
   "effect_on_headline": "excluding the byte counter: p36 res1eq vs res1 at w=1 is 1.075 (claimed 0.158), p36 res4dp vs res4 at w=0.1 is 0.870 (claimed 0.279), p37 res2eq vs res2 at w=1 is 1.140 (claimed 0.129), p37 res4eq vs res4 at w=0.1 is 0.743 (claimed 0.235); eq is >= baseline at w=1 in all six (curve,B) cells (1.075-1.140); w=0 headlines unchanged",
   "recommendation": "state w>0 figures as 'band as built, includes table bytes priced as operations'; report the byte-excluded band beside it; do not claim eq beats baseline at w=1 as an operation-count improvement; fix by renaming the counter (e.g. residual_table_bytes) so it is a shape counter, in a new study, not by editing these records"
  },
  {
   "id": "F2",
   "severity": "medium",
   "scope": "distance to rho at w > 0",
   "finding": "rho's per-step native work other than canonicalisation (cycle-window scan, jump index, distinguished-point test) is not in its counters, while candidates are charged a DP test (and eq an orientation read and 0.5 negation) per step; rho is the more incomplete lower bound, so the distance to rho at w > 0 is overstated for candidates",
   "effect": "charging rho one DP test per step (counters.steps) gives p36 res1eq 1.54/1.61/1.80 and res1dp 2.13/1.97/1.50 at w = 0/0.1/1 (harness: 1.54/1.75/2.66 and 2.13/2.14/2.22); the ordering rho ahead of every arm at w=0 is unaffected, at w=1 res1dp stays above rho (1.50)"
  },
  {
   "id": "F3",
   "severity": "low",
   "scope": "A/A control",
   "finding": "res2aa equals res2 to the last bit because counts are deterministic; the control cannot detect noise or bias in counts, only that arm label and run order do not matter"
  },
  {
   "id": "F4",
   "severity": "low",
   "scope": "C1 tally",
   "finding": "validator intervals (bootstrap and linearised t) find dp failing at w=0 in 2 of 6 cells (p36 res1dp, p37 res2dp); the harness-recorded intervals used by the producer add p37 res4dp (upper limit 1.002). Verdict 'C1 not met' holds either way; eq holds in 6/6 cells at harness pricing and fails at w=1 in all 6 once the byte counter is excluded (F1)"
  }
 ],
